&lt;li&gt;Lead end-to-end execution of a global portfolio of Tier 1 and Tier 2 third-party and proprietary events, translating global strategy into detailed plans, timelines, and deliverables.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own planning and delivery of industry conferences, sponsorships, hosted experiences, and proprietary programs across regions, ensuring consistent, high-quality execution aligned to global standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally with Product Marketing, Growth Marketing, Field Marketing, Content, Design, Sales, SDRs, and Marketing Operations to operationalize integrated event campaigns and ensure alignment with go-to-market priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive event programs that generate measurable pipeline and customer engagement through meeting programs, lead capture, attendee journeys, and coordinated post-event follow-up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage execution of global sponsorship programs, ensuring fulfillment of contractual deliverables including booths, staffing plans, capture frameworks, speaking engagements, customer events, and executive activations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Oversee agencies and vendors responsible for production, logistics, shipping, and on-site delivery, ensuring seamless and on-brand event experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Manage event budgets, forecasting, and spend tracking to deliver programs efficiently and within approved investment levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead project management across complex workstreams, driving alignment, accountability, and clear communication among stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Develop and maintain scalable processes, templates, and workflows that enable consistent global execution and improve operational efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;• Provide day-to-day guidance and mentorship to event managers and coordinators, supporting prioritization, workload management, and professional development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Marketing Operations to track performance, measure pipeline influence, and deliver post-event reporting and insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously evaluate programs to improve attendee experience, operational rigor, and overall program effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Other duties as assigned&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of B2B marketing experience, specifically in Tier 1 global industry events, Demand Generation, or Field Marketing with an enterprise focus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record driving pipeline creation, acceleration, and revenue impact in high-growth environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of executive-level engagement and tailoring messaging for complex buying committees and large-scale deals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience using Salesforce and Tableau to analyze pipeline health and provide executive reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Exceptional ability to navigate ambiguity, lead cross-functional teams, and build processes from the ground up.&lt;/li&gt;
